              "imageUrl": "https://img.evbuc.com/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc.com%2Fimages%2F1192241930%2F281899817652%2F1%2Foriginal.20260830-225541?h=294&w=294&auto=format%2Ccompress&q=75&sharp=10&rect=135%2C0%2C314%2C314&s=00bb20904029ec0f382c676969b64e83",
              "fullSizeImageUrl": "https://img.evbuc.com/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc.com%2Fimages%2F1192241930%2F281899817652%2F1%2Foriginal.20260830-225541?auto=format%2Ccompress&q=75&sharp=10&rect=135%2C0%2C314%2C314&s=97007e22bc036d706bb077af73ee55cb",
              "role": "headliner",
              "socialMedia": [],
              "bio": "Acclaimed British artist, filmmaker and creative director Nick Egan has helped shape the visual language of punk, new wave, fashion, rock and Britpop for more than four decades.\n\nEmerging from London’s original punk scene, he worked alongside Malcolm McLaren and Vivienne Westwood before creating influential artwork, graphic design and films for artists including The Clash, Duran Duran, INXS, The Cult and Oasis."
            },
            {
              "id": "11078753",
              "name": "Catalina  Guirado ",
              "tagline": "90s Cool Britannia It Girl · Creative Director · Curator",
              "imageUrl": "https://img.evbuc.com/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc.com%2Fimages%2F1192244174%2F281899817652%2F1%2Foriginal.20260831-000636?h=294&w=294&auto=format%2Ccompress&q=75&sharp=10&rect=227%2C146%2C1093%2C1093&s=114ed12ef2c8fcc74afacd7a47b9bd97",
              "fullSizeImageUrl": "https://img.evbuc.com/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc.com%2Fimages%2F1192244174%2F281899817652%2F1%2Foriginal.20260831-000636?auto=format%2Ccompress&q=75&sharp=10&rect=227%2C146%2C1093%2C1093&s=373f01acb42b894152ed86283ea42c75",
              "role": "supporter",
              "socialMedia": [],
              "bio": "Catalina Guirado is a British-Spanish creative director, designer, curator, and former model and television personality who became a defining face of 90s Cool Britannia. She is best remembered by British television audiences as The Gorgeous Girl—Chris Evans’s glamorous sidekick on Channel 4’s iconic TFI Friday.\n\nThrough Guirado Design Studio, Catalina’s work spans textile design, digital art and immersive experiences that bring together visual art, sound, frequency and wellbeing.\n\nFor more than fifteen years, Catalina has also worked as Creative Director of the Guirado Estate, overseeing and curating international museum and foundation exhibitions dedicated to the work of her father, Spanish artist Juan Antonio Guirado.\n\nCatalina curates and hosts Sartorial Correctness with Nick Egan: Creative Vandal — Live Forever: The Extended Remix."
            }
          ]
        },
